[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The SAA fixed income investment management questionnaire asks the firm to indicate whether it offers certain administrative and reporting services, and to state any additional fee and approximate amount for each. The relevant services are explicitly listed in the questionnaire section on administration.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Services and extra fees.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the fixed income investment management services questionnaire, the firm is asked to indicate whether it offers each of the following services and, if so, whether any additional fee is incurred and the approximate amount:

- Schedule D investment accounting
- Asset/liability management (dynamic financial analysis)
- Performance attribution
- Daily internet access of portfolio information
- SVO filing

The questionnaire presents these under a format of:
- Service
- Service Offered? Yes/No
- Approximate Fee

So the firm must identify for each listed service both availability and any added charge.</CONTENT>
